.el .ds Aq '
.TH devin-plugins-install 1  "install " 
.SH NAME
devin\-plugins\-install \- Install a plugin from a source (auto\-installs its required plugins)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdevin plugins install\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install a plugin from a source (auto\-installs its required plugins).
.PP
A source is a GitHub `owner/repo`, a git URL, or a local path. Append `#path/to/plugin` when the plugin is below a git repository\*(Aqs root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the interactive trust prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
Install on this machine only, without adding the plugin to your personal plugins
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>
The plugin source (e.g. `acme/review\-tools`, `acme/plugins#plugins/review`, a git URL, or `./path`)
